  "Graphing patterns": ["Graphing Patterns", "Turn a number pattern into points and graph them.", ["Make a table of the pattern.", "Each column gives an ordered pair.", "Plot the points; a steady rule makes a straight line."], "Rule: y = x + 2. Graph x = 0, 1, 2, 3.", ["The pairs are (0, 2), (1, 3), (2, 4), (3, 5).", "Plot each point.", "They line up in a straight line."], "Check each point against the rule.", { type: "coord", points: [{ x: 0, y: 2 }, { x: 1, y: 3 }, { x: 2, y: 4 }, { x: 3, y: 5 }], line: true }],
  "Classifying shapes": ["Classifying Shapes", "Shapes belong to families based on their sides and angles.", ["A quadrilateral has 4 sides.", "A parallelogram has 2 pairs of parallel sides.", "A rectangle is a parallelogram with 4 right angles.", "A rhombus has 4 equal sides; a square is both a rectangle and a rhombus."], "Is a square a rectangle?", ["A rectangle needs 4 right angles.", "A square has 4 right angles.", "So yes, every square is a rectangle."], "Draw a family tree: quadrilateral → parallelogram → rectangle and rhombus → square.", { type: "polygon", kind: "rhombus" }],
